{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-sonnet-5","packSha":"883217ec1a57f45fa21ad39f26229a3a81b85d5b1bb9b474448a9a7da2eb55fd","packTokens":5037,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":54,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":4956,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the invoice reminders API shall return every invoice that has the open status and a due date and for which today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days).\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-08, and an open invoice INV-1 has due date 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response is 200 and contains INV-1\",\n    \"Given threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-07, and an open invoice INV-2 has due date 2026-09-01 (6 days past due) when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response does not contain INV-2\",\n    \"Given business timezone is UTC+2, the current UTC time is 2026-09-07T23:30Z (local date 2026-09-08), threshold is 7, and an open invoice INV-3 has due date 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response contains INV-3\",\n    \"Given the overdue threshold setting is changed to 10, today is 2026-10-15, and open invoices are due 2026-10-05 and 2026-10-06 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response contains the invoice due 2026-10-05 and does not contain the invoice due 2026-10-06\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If an invoice has any status other than open in the existing invoice data (including paid, closed, void, cancelled, draft or written off) or has no due date, then the invoice reminders API shall leave it out of the overdue list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given invoices C (paid), D (closed), E (void) and F (draft) are each 30 days past their due date, and open invoice G has no due date when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then none of C, D, E, F or G is in the response\",\n    \"Given invoice INV-6 is in the overdue list and its status is then changed to paid or closed in the invoice data when GET the overdue list endpoint is called again with a valid staff token then the response no longer contains INV-6, with no other action needed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The invoice reminders API shall work out overdue status at query time without writing any overdue flag or status to invoice records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given a snapshot of all invoice rows in Postgres is taken, and some of those invoices are overdue when the overdue list endpoint and the invoice detail endpoint for an overdue invoice are called then every invoice row is byte-for-byte unchanged compared with the snapshot (no status or updated-at column written)\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested, the invoice reminders API shall return, for each overdue invoice, its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue, where days overdue is the number of whole calendar days from the due date to today in the business timezone.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given today is 2026-10-15 in the business timezone and open invoice INV-100 for customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, is due 2026-10-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response's INV-100 entry has invoice number INV-100, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01 and days overdue 14\",\n    \"Given today is 2026-09-08, threshold is 7 and open invoice INV-1 is due 2026-09-01 when GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token then the response's INV-1 entry has days overdue 7\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given customer A has 2 overdue invoices and customer B has 3 overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested filtered by customer A then the response contains exactly customer A's 2 overdue invoices\",\n    \"Given customer C has no overdue invoices when the overdue list is requested filtered by customer C then the response is 200 with an empty list\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter of 7–30, 31–60, 61–90 or 91 and over (90+), the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue falls inside that bucket, bounds included.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoices with days overdue 7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90 and 91 when the overdue list is requested with each bucket in turn then the 7–30 response contains 7 and 30; 31–60 contains 31 and 60; 61–90 contains 61 and 90; 90+ contains only 91\",\n    \"Given customer A has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days and customer B has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days when the overdue list is requested with customer A and bucket 31–60 then the response contains only customer A's 40-day invoice\",\n    \"Given any data when the overdue list is requested with a bucket value that is not one of the four buckets (e.g. 5-9) then the response is 400 and names the allowed bucket values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a request to the overdue list, invoice detail or send-reminder endpoint has no valid staff authentication under the existing API's authentication scheme, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401, return no invoice or customer data, and send no email.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given no authentication credentials when the overdue list, invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints are each called then each response is 401 with no invoice or customer fields in the body, the email provider stub receives no request, and no reminder history row is created\",\n    \"Given an expired or invalid staff token and an overdue invoice when the overdue list endpoint and the send-reminder endpoint for that invoice are called then both responses are 401 and the email provider stub receives no call\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user sends a reminder for an overdue invoice whose customer has an email address, the invoice reminders API shall send one email through the configured transactional email provider to the single email address on the customer record, using the configured template and containing the invoice number, amount and due date.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-100 (amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01) belongs to a customer with email accounts@crumb.example, and a stubbed email provider when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 2xx and the provider stub receives exactly one send request addressed to accounts@crumb.example whose body contains 'INV-100', '250.00' and '2026-10-01'\",\n    \"Given the template in configuration is changed to a different subject line when the send-reminder endpoint for an overdue invoice is called with a valid staff token then the send request received by the email provider stub has the new subject line\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the customer record of the invoice has no email address, then the invoice reminders API shall reject the send-reminder request with HTTP 422 and an error saying the customer has no email address, without calling the email provider or recording a reminder history entry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-200 belongs to a customer whose email field is empty when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-200 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 422 with a message saying the customer has no email address, the provider stub receives no request, and no reminder history row is created\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a send-reminder request is for an invoice that is not currently overdue, then the invoice reminders API shall reject the request with HTTP 409 and an error saying the invoice is not overdue, without calling the email provider.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given invoice INV-21 has status paid when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-21 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 409 saying the invoice is not overdue, and the email provider stub receives no request\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a reminder send is attempted with the email provider, the invoice reminders API shall store a reminder history entry holding the invoice, the authenticated staff user who sent it, the UTC timestamp of the attempt, and a delivery status of sent or failed with a failure reason when failed.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given staff user 'sam' is authenticated, INV-100 is overdue with a valid customer email, and the provider stub accepts the send when sam sends a reminder for INV-100 at 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z then a reminder history row exists for INV-100 with sender 'sam', timestamp 2026-10-15T09:30:00Z (±5 s), status 'sent' and an empty failure reason\",\n    \"Given INV-100 is overdue with a valid customer email and the provider stub accepts sends when 'maria' and then 'tom' each call the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 more than 60 seconds apart then two separate reminder history rows exist for INV-100 with senders 'maria' and 'tom', each with its own timestamp\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If the email provider returns an error or does not respond within the 8-second send timeout when a reminder is sent, then the invoice reminders API shall record the attempt as failed with the provider's reason or a timeout reason, return an error response containing that reason, and keep the invoice on the overdue list.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-100 and a provider stub that rejects the send with 'invalid recipient' when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token then the response is 502 including 'invalid recipient', a reminder history row for INV-100 has status 'failed' and reason 'invalid recipient', and the overdue list response still contains INV-100\",\n    \"Given overdue invoice INV-100 and a provider stub that does not respond within 8 seconds when the send-reminder endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token then an error response saying the send timed out is returned within 10 seconds, and a reminder history row for INV-100 has status 'failed' with a reason saying it timed out\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If a send-reminder request for an invoice arrives within 60 seconds of an earlier accepted send-reminder request for the same invoice, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 409 as a duplicate, without calling the email provider or recording another reminder history entry.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given INV-100 is overdue with a valid customer email when two send-reminder requests for INV-100 are sent 1 second apart then the first returns 2xx, the second returns 409, the provider stub receives exactly one send request, and exactly one reminder history row exists for INV-100\",\n    \"Given a reminder for INV-100 was accepted at 09:00:00 when another send-reminder request for INV-100 arrives at 09:01:01 then the response is 2xx, the provider stub receives a second send request and a second reminder history row is recorded\",\n    \"Given a reminder for INV-100 was accepted 10 seconds ago when a send-reminder request for a different overdue invoice INV-101 is made then the INV-101 response is 2xx and the provider stub receives a send request for INV-101\",\n    \"Given two send-reminder requests for INV-100 sent at the same moment when both are processed then the provider stub receives exactly one send request and the other response is 409\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests an invoice's detail, the invoice reminders API shall return the invoice number, customer, amount, due date, whether it is overdue, and its full reminder history newest first, where each entry shows the sender, timestamp, delivery status and failure reason if there is one.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given INV-100 with amount 250.00, due 2026-10-01, one 'sent' attempt by jo at 2026-10-08T09:00Z and one 'failed' attempt by sam at 2026-10-09T10:00Z with reason 'invalid recipient' when the invoice detail endpoint for INV-100 is called with a valid staff token then the response has invoice number, customer, amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01, the overdue indicator, and history [sam 2026-10-09T10:00Z failed 'invalid recipient', jo 2026-10-08T09:00Z sent with no reason] in that order\",\n    \"Given an invoice with no reminders when the invoice detail endpoint for it is called with a valid staff token then the response has an empty reminder history\",\n    \"Given invoice id 'does-not-exist' when the invoice detail endpoint is called for it with a valid staff token then the response is 404\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d1 sizing).\",\n  \"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d2/d3 sizing).\",\n  \"The send-reminder endpoint gives the staff user a result within a fixed time, including when the email provider is slow. This is the single send-timeout budget REQ-12 uses.\",\n  \"Customer email addresses (PII) are not written to application logs.\",\n  \"Every reminder attempt is kept for audit.\",\n  \"No duplicate emails come from double submits.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}